            <ArticleTitle>Prosthetic aortic valve abscess producing total right coronary artery occlusion: diagnosis by transesophageal three-dimensional echocardiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>395-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a patient with total right coronary artery occlusion produced by a prosthetic aortic valve abscess. The diagnosis was made by transesophageal three-dimensional echocardiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
